{
  "requirement": "When given `--path <crate-dir>` and no existing Habeas dev dependency, `habeas setup` MUST add that local crate as the dev dependency. Repeating setup MUST NOT add a duplicate Habeas dependency.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Judgment:** the implementation and tests meet `requirements.cli.setup_local_path`, and I found no unmarked behavior.\n\n**Implementation**\n- `src/main.rs` defines `habeas setup --path <crate-dir>` with clap as `Setup { path: Option<PathBuf> }`. It dispatches `Command::Setup { path } => setup::run(path.as_deref())`.\n- `setup::run` in `src/setup.rs` (lines 92–189) parses `Cargo.toml` and calls `has_habeas_dev_dependency`. That helper (lines 25–33) looks for `habeas` under `[dev-dependencies]`. Both carry `{impl}` references to this requirement.\n- When no Habeas dev dependency exists, `run` executes `cargo add --dev habeas --manifest-path <root>/Cargo.toml`.\n  - If `--path` was given, it appends `--path <canonicalized crate dir>`.\n  - So the local crate is added as the dev dependency, and a relative `--path` resolves from the invocation directory.\n  - A cargo failure becomes an error.\n  - A missing crate directory makes `fs::canonicalize` fail before any file is written.\n- When a Habeas dev dependency already exists, `cargo add` is skipped. A repeated setup therefore adds no duplicate and leaves `Cargo.toml` untouched.\n- The `--path` option definition itself sits under the `requirements.cli.clap` marker on the `Command` enum. That is an interface declaration, not separate behavior, so I don't count it as a marking gap.\n- The code does only what the requirement and the other setup requirements it carries (`cli.setup`, `cli.setup_css`, `cli.setup_project`, `cli.mdbook`) specify. I found no unmarked extra behavior.\n\n**Tests** (`tests/setup.rs`)\n- `local_path_setup_adds_exactly_that_crate_once` uses a relative `--path`.\n  - It asserts exactly one `habeas` entry across the dependency tables, located in `dev-dependencies`.\n  - It asserts the entry's `path` resolves to the requested crate directory.\n  - It reruns setup and asserts `Cargo.toml` is byte-for-byte unchanged.\n- `local_path_setup_keeps_an_existing_habeas_dev_dependency` starts with `habeas = \"0.1\"` already in `[dev-dependencies]`. After setup with `--path`, the manifest is unchanged: no replacement and no duplicate.\n- `local_path_setup_rejects_a_missing_crate_directory` is the failure case. Setup exits non-zero, `Cargo.toml` is unchanged, and no Habeas dependency is added.\n- `setup_is_repeatable` runs setup twice with `--path` and checks that the manifest has a path dependency.\n- The `habeas_dependencies` helper is marked `{test}` and is used by these tests.\n\nThese cover the main cases: add, repeat, an existing dependency, a relative path, and an invalid path. Dependency forms outside `[dev-dependencies]` aren't tested, but the requirement doesn't ask about them.\n\nThere are no acknowledged FIXMEs or other gaps.",
  "references": "fd7a5c300f8e17c687db4aa9c55a2a4280e3e94348e60d3b48ed61e09ceb4e8f",
